.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_CHECK_PRIVATE_KEY 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_check_private_key ,
.Nm X509_REQ_check_private_key
.Nd check the consistency of a private key with the public key in an X509 certificate or certificate request
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_check_private_key
.Fa "const X509 *cert"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_check_private_key
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_check_private_key
function checks the consistency of private key
.Fa pkey
with the public key in
.Fa cert .
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_check_private_key
is equivalent to
.Fn X509_check_private_key
except that
.Fa req
represents a certificate request of structure
.Vt X509_REQ .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_check_private_key
and
.Fn X509_REQ_check_private_key
return 1 if the keys match each other, and 0 if not.
.Pp
If the key is invalid or an error occurred, the reason code can be
obtained using
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Sh BUGS
The
.Fn X509_check_private_key
and
.Fn X509_REQ_check_private_key
functions do not check if
.Fa pkey
itself is indeed a private key or not.
They merely compare the public materials (e.g., exponent and modulus of
an RSA key) and/or key parameters (e.g.
EC params of an EC key) of a key pair.
So they also return success if
.Fa pkey
is a matching public key.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3
